// A character: her body, stats and relationship, values that track the
// friendship, a presence line, a talk menu and an actions menu whose options
// depend on those values, a quest with several stages, and a scene scheduled
// to play a few actions later. The interface shows Talk, Actions, Look and
// Smell buttons for her while the player is in the same place.

== character wren
name: Wren
pronouns: she
lives at: clearing
description:
    A small, weathered woman in a patched green coat, whittling something that might become a bird. [if wren.trust is at least friendly]She hums while she works.[end if]
// The Smell button.
scent: Woodsmoke and pine resin.
// A line added to the place's description while she is there.
presence: Wren sits by the lean-to, whittling.
// Her body, fighting numbers and relationship start at these values; scenes
// read and change them like any value: wren.scale, wren.level, wren.met.
// "wren is female" reads her body, as it does for the player.
body:
    scale: 2
    weight: 3
    definition: 6
    androgyny: 6
stats:
    level: 3
    max hp: 30
    perception: 16
relationship:
    met: no
// Other things to do with her (the Actions button), written like a menu.
actions:
    title: What do you want to do?
    leave: Never mind
    * Help with firewood -- Carry an armful of wood to her fire
        You stack the wood by the lean-to. Wren nods her thanks.
        if wren.trust is wary:
            ~ wren.trust = friendly
        ~ spend 1 turn
    * Share some berries -- Offer her your wild berries [if player has wild_berries]
        ~ take wild_berries
        Wren eats them one at a time, slowly, as if they were sweets.
// Values belong to the character and are saved with the game.
// A list of states is in order, so "wren.trust is at least friendly" works.
values:
    trust: wary, friendly, trusted
    heard_story: flag
    visits: number
talk:
    ~ wren.visits + 1 quietly
    ~ wren.met = yes quietly
    [if wren.trust is wary]Wren looks up. 'Oh. A visitor.'[else if wren.trust is friendly]Wren smiles. 'Back again?'[else]Wren pats the stone beside her. 'Sit, sit.'[end if]
    -> wren.talk

// The quest: its stages in order, each with its journal line. The first stage
// is the start. The journal shows it once it passes its first stage.
== quest lost_knife
name: Wren's knife
region: woods
stages:
    not_started
    asked: Wren lost her carving knife somewhere in the forest.
    returned: You gave Wren her knife back.
    shared_supper: Wren shared her supper with you. You have a friend in the woods.
done at: shared_supper

// The talk menu. Options: "* Label -- description [if condition]".
// The menu shows again after each option, until the player leaves; an option
// with [then leave] closes it.
== menu wren.talk
title: What do you want to talk about?
leave: Say goodbye
pause after each: yes
leave text: Wren goes back to her whittling.

* The woods -- Ask about the forest
    -> wren.about_woods
* Anything you need? -- Offer to help [if quest lost_knife is not_started]
    'I dropped my carving knife somewhere in the forest. Can't find it anywhere.'
    ~ quest lost_knife = asked
* Return the knife -- Hand over the carving knife [if quest lost_knife is asked and player has carving_knife]
    ~ take carving_knife
    ~ quest lost_knife = returned
    ~ wren.trust = friendly
    'My knife!' Wren turns it over in her hands. 'Here, take this for your trouble.'
    ~ give herbal_tea
    // A scene that plays after three more actions, wherever the player is.
    ~ schedule wren.invitation after 3 actions
* Supper -- Join Wren for supper [if quest lost_knife is returned and time is night] [then leave]
    -> wren.supper
* The shed key -- Ask about the padlocked shed [if wren.trust is at least friendly and not player has shed_key]
    'That old shed? The key's under the third stone.' She digs it out and hands it over.
    ~ give shed_key

== scene wren.about_woods
// "player has visited X": the player has been to that place.
if player has visited old_bridge and not wren.heard_story:
    'You've been down to the old bridge? Then you've seen the mist,' Wren says. 'Don't follow it unless you mean to leave for good.'
if not wren.heard_story:
    'The foxes here are odd,' Wren says. 'Lose a scuffle with one and you might grow a tail.'
    ~ wren.heard_story = yes quietly
else:
    Wren shrugs. '[one of]Stay on the path.[or]The foxes like the clearing at dusk.[or]Mind the brambles by the river.[at random]'

== scene wren.invitation
A paper bird flutters down beside you, folded from birch bark. Inside, in careful letters: *Supper at the clearing, after dark. W.*

== scene wren.supper
Wren stirs a pot of mushroom stew over a small fire. You eat in comfortable silence while the stars come out.
---
'Not bad company,' she says at last. 'For a visitor.'
~ eat 30
~ quest lost_knife = shared_supper
~ wren.trust = trusted
